From 6aeb1e74e1881688c865a819e737310ebefc2f42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nadia Rodionova <273119990+sosidudku1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:16:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] os.web.crawl: unzip gzipped sitemaps, follow a same-site
 start redirect, handle JS-built pages (ATO-970)

Sitemaps are fetched as raw bytes and unzipped with node zlib under a 10 MB
cap, whether the file is .xml.gz, typed application/(x-)gzip or sent with
Content-Encoding: gzip. A start page that redirects within the same site
(www/apex, http/https, same registrable domain) moves the crawl there after
reading the new host's robots.txt; another site stops the crawl and says
where it went. Off-site redirect hops are no longer requested. Pages that
are JavaScript shells are rendered in the agent's own browser (the fetch
ladder's renderer, at most 5 per crawl, paced) or listed as needing
browser.navigate.

(cherry picked from commit 0a076b47cc9f7a358bbf5f5d1bc3c141fb2f5417)
